# The reference checkout, cloned for porting and differential testing.
#
# ANCHORED with a leading slash, and it matters: an unanchored pattern matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth. The `parser/` entry that used to sit here
# for the moonbitlang/parser checkout silently swallowed `lib/syntax/parser/` --
# `moon package` walks the tree gitignore-aware, so the published zip came out
# with no parser package in it at all. `moon publish --dry-run` is what caught
# that; keep running it before a release.
/wax/

# MoonBit build output
_build/
target/
.mooncakes/
*.mbt.map.json

# Pinned reference binary (13 MB; restore with tools/fetch-reference.sh,
# which verifies it against the sha256 in tools/reference.json)
tools/wax-linux-x86_64
tools/SHA256SUMS

# Harness output. test/corpus/ and test/golden/ are deliberately COMMITTED:
# they make the differential suite hermetic (no wax checkout, no npm reference
# needed to run it) and turn reference drift into a reviewable diff.
test/report/
